# Context

## Background
Workstream 3 of the upstream-alignment plan: port the PR #67
leftovers 4c6ed8d (harden performance recovery flows) and
8f98027 (guard prewarmed project rendering) onto the fork's
signed-session playback layer. 2bffb78 was skipped per plan.

## Why This Way
- Upstream's buildMuxPlaybackHlsUrl change (drop
  min_resolution=720p) touches an unsigned stream.mux.com
  builder. The fork has no client URL builder, and
  convex/muxPlayback.ts (which still sets min_resolution) is
  outside this workstream's file ownership, so it was left
  for the convex-file owner.
- Upstream's grant-failure retry card was mapped to the fork's
  bootstrap state machine: the card only replaces the
  "bootstrapping" spinner, because password and throttle
  states already have their own recovery UI.
- The retry backoff exists because VideoPlayer reports an
  access error only once per attached source. A failed
  keep-alive refresh would otherwise never retry: the session
  state is unchanged, so the refresh timer never re-arms.
- The project-data guard lives in useProjectData rather than
  the page: the crash (project._id inside videos.map while the
  project document is still loading) is only reachable when a
  prewarmed videos.list resolves before projects.get.

## Gotchas
- Concurrent workstreams share this working tree. Validation
  for this commit ran in a throwaway git worktree of HEAD plus
  only this diff, because sibling edits briefly broke
  typecheck mid-session.

